          "timeDisplay": "January 7, 2026",
          "category": "Natural Disasters",
          "categoryClass": "natural-disasters",
          "borderColor": "#c77d10",
          "headline": "Magnitude 6.4 Earthquake Strikes Davao Oriental",
          "headlineHref": "/interactive-timeline/index.html?date=2026-01-07&search=Magnitude%206.4%20Earthquake%20Strikes%20Davao%20Oriental",
          "descriptionHtml": "<p>A magnitude 6.4 earthquake struck 28 km northeast of Manay, Davao Oriental, at 11:02 a.m., an aftershock of the November 28, 2025 magnitude 7.5 quake. PHIVOLCS said more than 11.7 million people felt it, with intensity VI in the nearest towns. DSWD began monitoring damage in a province still recovering from last year's shock.</p>",
          "sourceLinks": [
            {
              "label": "volcanodiscovery.com",
              "href": "https://www.volcanodiscovery.com/earthquakes/quake-info/22585867/quake-felt-Jan-7-2026-Near-General-Santos-Soccsksargen-Philippines.html"
