          "descriptionHtml": "<p>The Traslacion from Quirino Grandstand to Quiapo Church lasted 30 hours, 50 minutes — the longest on record — as 9.6 million devotees joined the nine-day novena. Four deaths were reported. Bishop Rufino Sescon used the feast to urge humility amid the flood-control scandal, and President Marcos declared January 9 a special non-working day in Manila.</p>",
